  "problem": "L-meta-652",
  "generator": "matching_synthesis.py",
  "checker": "lrat-trim rel-0.2.0",
  "proof_format": "gzip-compressed binary LRAT. Regenerate each CNF with its arguments and replace CNF with a local pathname. Verify the decompressed proof against that CNF.",
  "basis": [
    "An 11-gate encoding is unsatisfiable on inputs with at most one true bit on each side.",
    "Fixing any input true leaves a restriction of size at least 11. Fixing it false leaves a restriction of size at least 9. Input permutations, a simultaneous reflection, and transposition cover all six inputs.",
    "Constant propagation under a pin eliminates every gate with a constant operand. The remaining circuit must meet the corresponding restricted lower bound.",
    "A 12-gate circuit for the full task would satisfy the true-pin bounds even when its output tests are limited to the 16 sparse rows. This strengthened instance is unsatisfiable.",
    "Number edges by 3*color+left, with right=(left+color) mod 3. Precompute each listed set of raw products, then allow all six raw inputs and those products in the tail. All five-product representatives exclude tail size nine. Thus at most four distinct direct products are possible at size fourteen.",
    "In each four-product case exclude additional raw products, using the previous result. Both pin bounds apply to the complete fourteen gates, including the four precomputed products. All seven cases are unsatisfiable.",
    "Representatives are lexicographically least under independent cyclic shifts of the left and right triples, simultaneous reflection, and optional interchange of the two sides.",
    "The LRAT checker validates the generated CNF. The reduction from the project circuit model to these CNF instances is an external argument."
  ],
